@* The navigation column (VISUAL_DESIGN.md §6): Fluent's nav on Surface 1 with small items. The active item keeps Fluent's
   accent indicator and semibold text, and gets GFO's Accent soft background through the ActiveClass parameter. Shown
   while a league is open. M0 has Home and Settings; the league sections arrive with their features. Items are Fluent's Small density (28 px), so the full
   league nav fits a 720 px window. The gutters and the indicator are GFO's, through the classes added here (the css). *@
<div class="gfo-main-nav">
    <FluentNav Class="gfo-nav" Width="100%" Density="NavDensity.Small" BackgroundColor="var(--colorNeutralBackground1)" BackgroundColorHover="var(--colorNeutralBackground2)">
    <NavEntry Href="@Routes.Home" Title="Home" Icon="IconName.Home" Match="NavLinkMatch.All" />
		<NavEntry Href="@Routes.Roster" Title="Roster" Icon="IconName.People" Match="NavLinkMatch.All" />
		<NavEntry Href="@Routes.League" Title="League" Icon="IconName.Board" Match="NavLinkMatch.All" />
		<NavEntry Href="@Routes.Settings" Title="Settings" Icon="IconName.Settings" />
    </FluentNav>
</div>
